Z||000007||Bob Englert||04-21-2001||10:40 AM||||I am not sure I want to say anything that might contribute to getting you or someone else on the road killed.<P>I have to agree with the other posts.  The Fiero is not a prepared race car, and driving the car at the speeds and way you describe on public roads is irresponsible and dangerous.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000008||Spektyr||04-21-2001||11:01 AM||||Well, for one thing you say that it isn't as good as it should be, and then use a Honda as the comparison.<P>While it is theoretically possible to make a Fiero handle in SOME ways like a Honda, you're talking about two very different cars.<P>The Fiero has four wheel independant suspension, rear-wheel drive and a mid-engine.<P>The Honda has... well the same suspension as practically every other small yuppie-mobile.<P>While both cars can be severely modified from their original incarnation, unless you're talking about some VERY serious custom work, the Fiero will never share the Front engine, front-wheel drive characteristics of the Honda.<P>Most of us think this is a good thing.  Not to mention your center of gravity is so low in a Fiero you'd have to TRY to roll it over.  Even then you'd probably fail.<P>My advice would be to get it diagnosed by a professional.  If that car has ever gotten wheels off the ground, you could have problems way beyond what we can diagnose here.  If you want a cheap diagnosis, take it in to get it aligned, the mechanics will normally point out every single thing they can see under the car that needs to be replaced (whether it does or not).||||reg||1
Z||000009||curtis||04-21-2001||03:03 PM||||I just had my suspension redone poly ball joints shocks all the way around. I also had a loud clunking over bumps. It turned out  it was one of the ball joints I was told they were prepacked with grease, but they weren't.||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||04-21-2001||08:57 PM||||84-87 cars can be made to handle much better than many of them do stock. <P>While being peaved,,,, I was being serious.... Fiero will never take that kind of abuse. you can replace parts till hell freezes. The car was never built for that type driving.<P>At the least you will need to totally rebuild the suspension. New bushings. new BJs. New struts. New Shocks. and very likely reworked or aftermarket control arms. May also need a whole diferant spring package.<P>Even after all that parts will bend/break jumping things. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||WKDFIRO||04-22-2001||02:05 PM||||Is that why my Charger is making so many noises?<P>I painted it orange and put a big 01 on the side but when I jump over rivers and cliffs and land it always starts making these funny noises?<P>Kidding aside, you are abusing the Fiero if only for 2 nights a week. <P>DID YOU THINK THAT A FORUM OF FIERO LOVERS WOULD NOT GIVE YOU GRIEF?<P>As for ideas, if you want to keep catching air driving it like you stole it two nights a week and hitting the triple digits, get a Honda. <P>Theres a billion more Hondas out there when you are done wasting the one you have. Who knows what you've done to that Fiero.||||reg||13
